Ludwerk: a lost D3D12 device crashes the first draw after a pipeline is bound.

0002 stopped SDL_PushGPU*UniformData dereferencing the NULL uniform buffer a
lost device hands back. The same NULL has a second way in. Binding a pipeline
acquires a uniform buffer for each of its slots that has none
(D3D12_BindGraphicsPipeline, D3D12_BindComputePipeline); on a lost device each
acquire fails -- "Failed to map buffer pool!", once a slot -- and leaves the
slot NULL. The next draw or dispatch then binds its root constant buffer
views from `uniformBuffers[i]->buffer`, and the process dies of an access
violation inside SDL.

Seen three times on hosted Windows runners, whose software device was removed
under a test: the message twice -- a vertex slot and a fragment slot --
and then the fault, every time.

The fix binds nothing for a slot that has no buffer. The draw goes nowhere --
there is no device to draw it -- and the error stays set, so the submit that
follows fails and the application is told its device is gone. Still present
upstream on 2026-10-12.

